    'Relational databases from the schema up: ER modeling, the relational model, SQL, joins, aggregation, normalization, integrity, indexes, transactions and isolation, SQL injection, a thin app layer (Python sqlite3 or Java JDBC), and a light look at query plans. Portfolio spine: a real schema plus a small SQL-backed app. SQLite is enough; you are not building CMU’s storage engine.',
